            <ArticleTitle>[A boy with a painful tumour of his skull].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A9939</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12-year-old boy presented with an increasing painful swelling of the skull. Physical examination revealed in the left parieto-occipital region a skin-coloured solid mass of 2-3 cm in diameter. The X-ray of the skull was highly suspicious for Langerhans cell histiocytosis. Histopathology of a biopsy of the lesion confirmed the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
